## What changed

The single Decision node (urgent/not) is replaced by a **Script → Switch** combo:

- **Script** independently scores both signals and outputs one of four priority strings: `vip_urgent`, `vip`, `urgent`, or `standard`
- **Switch** routes each email into its own lane — each with a distinct Slack message and customer reply

## The four lanes

| | Urgent keywords | No urgent keywords |
|---|---|---|
| **VIP sender** | 🔴 `vip_urgent` — Slack alert + priority reply | 🟡 `vip` — Slack alert + VIP reply |
| **Non-VIP** | 🟠 `urgent` — Slack alert + urgent reply | `standard` — auto-reply + mark read |

## Defaults I've baked in (all overridable via flow input variables)
- **Urgency keywords**: `urgent, outage, down, critical, broken, not working, emergency, ASAP, crash, refund, cancel, churn, legal, escalate, complaint, furious` — designed to catch both technical and emotional signals
- **VIP domains**: `acme.com, globex.com, initech.com, umbrella-corp.com, hooli.com` — placeholder names; you swap these for your real enterprise accounts before go-live

